## INCIDENT NOTICE -- 2026-08-29, caused by nexus-qa during the Phase 6 retry-1 re-QA dispatch

While updating this file's `pending_qa`/`last_qa_report`/`qa_retry_count` fields and appending a new decision-log entry (as instructed for this dispatch), a PowerShell scripting error (an invalid array-type cast on two `List<string>.AddRange()` calls, which failed silently mid-script rather than halting it) caused the ENTIRE prior contents of this file -- every line of the original ~400-line file, including the FULL decision log spanning every phase of every initiative this project has run (nextbot-plan.md's original phases, the client-feedback-batch initiative, the platform-manager-console work, and Phases 0-6 of the current Target Architecture Blueprint) -- to be overwritten with only the single new decision-log entry being added at the time. This was an unintended, purely mechanical scripting bug, not a deliberate edit, and not sanctioned by any instruction this agent received.

**Recovery attempted and exhausted, all unsuccessful**: this directory is not a git repository (confirmed -- no `.git` anywhere under `d:\work\products\nextbot`, unlike sibling projects on the same machine); Windows Volume Shadow Copy is inaccessible without administrator privileges (`vssadmin`/`Get-CimInstance Win32_ShadowCopy` both failed); VS Code's local-history feature (`%APPDATA%\Code\User\History`) holds no entries for this specific file; OneDrive does not sync this path (`D:\work\products\nextbot` is outside the synced OneDrive folder, which is otherwise empty); no other on-disk copy of this file exists anywhere on the machine (`NEXUS_STATE.md` files exist for two sibling projects, `exam-4u` and `LiveAvatar`, but those are unrelated files for different projects).

**What was salvaged**: the metadata header above (lines that were short enough to have been fully captured in this session's own tool output before the corruption) was reconstructed with high confidence, EXCEPT `active_dev_plan`'s full value, which was truncated. This one new decision-log entry (Phase 6 retry 1 re-QA, below) is complete and accurate -- it is this dispatch's own genuine output, not a reconstruction. **Everything else that was in this file's decision log -- every dev/qa entry for every prior phase of every prior initiative -- is gone and NOT reproduced here, because fabricating plausible-sounding historical entries from a QA agent's partial memory would be actively misleading, not helpful.**

**Recommended recovery path for the orchestrator/user**: (1) the orchestrator's own conversation context very likely still holds the full, accurate content of this file from when it was last read to construct this dispatch's prompt -- that is almost certainly the fastest, most reliable way to restore it verbatim; (2) `docs/plans/*.md` (`target-architecture-blueprint-plan.md`, `nextbot-plan.md`, `client-feedback-batch-plan.md`, `iam-sso-scim-service-accounts-plan.md`, `mcp-enrolment-wizard-plan.md`, `platform-manager-console-plan.md`, `chakra-to-shadcn-plan.md`) are all UNTOUCHED by this incident and duplicate a substantial fraction of the same decision content in prose -- a solid secondary source for the Target Architecture Blueprint's Phases 0-6 specifically; (3) every `qa-results/**/REPORT.md` file on disk is untouched -- only this state file's index of them was lost, not the reports themselves; (4) strongly recommend this project adopt version control (`git init` + regular commits) going forward specifically so a future accidental overwrite of this file is a `git checkout` away from being fixed, not a permanent loss.

