## Orchestrator-reconstructed history (2026-08-29, after the incident above)

The section below is reconstructed by the orchestrating Claude session from its own conversation history, since the original verbatim decision log (every individual dev/qa dispatch entry across this project's whole run) was destroyed by the incident documented above and cannot be recovered byte-for-byte. This is a narrative summary at the level of "what shipped and what it took to get it QA-green," not a restoration of every original entry's exact wording. Treat the individual plan docs and `qa-results/**/REPORT.md` files (all untouched by the incident) as the authoritative detailed record; this section exists so a future dispatch has continuity without having to re-derive the whole project history from scratch.

**Original Nexus pipeline (this project's first build)**: SaaS multi-tenant conversational AI platform. Specification -> Architecture (HLD/LLD/ADR-0001 through ADR-0008) -> phased Development covering auth/RBAC/MFA, MCP connectors + Tool Catalog + tiered approval (Tier 1/2/3), the Agent Platform (definitions/versions/eval suites/model gateway v1/runtime traces), conversations/escalations/approval queue, Settings & Security screens, Users & Roles, Audit Log, the customer-facing widget, PII/guardrails/retention/DSR compliance screens -> QA (many phases, the standard dev-QA retry loop) -> Deployment (docker-compose.yml, seed script, Dockerfiles) -> Final Review (full-regression QA pass, green). docs/PRODUCT_SPECIFICATION.md, docs/BACKLOG.md, docs/architecture/HLD.md/LLD.md, ADR-0001 through ADR-0008 all date from this phase and remain the base the later work built on.

**Chakra UI to shadcn/ui migration** (mid-project, user-requested): replaced Chakra with shadcn/ui + Tailwind + Base UI across the Admin Console and widget, per a shadcn theme preset the user supplied. ADR-0010 records this (with a correction to two factual errors in ADR-0002 4.2a about Chakra's actual version/library). Ran in batches (A-D) with several real QA-caught defects along the way (a Chakra focus-ring shim leaking globally, a WCAG contrast failure on status badges, breadcrumb 404s on routes with no index page, a Select primitive not resolving preset values) -- all fixed and closed. docs/plans/chakra-to-shadcn-plan.md has the detail.

**Platform Manager console** (user-requested, NFR-11's previously-unbuilt "Platform Operator" persona): a pragmatic-MVP cross-tenant operator console inside apps/web (not a separate app), gated by an operator token + IP allowlist, not a tenant login. Built in 3 phases (auth+tenant CRUD+audit trail; status/plan-tier management; cross-tenant MCP health rollup, metadata-only per NFR-11). The single hardest, longest-running defect in the whole project's history lived here: making a denied request to this console's pages byte-for-byte indistinguishable from a genuinely missing page. This took 4 dev rounds and 5 QA rounds on the API side (finally solved by making both "denied" and "genuinely missing" call the literal same static response-generating function, rather than any imitation/mirroring strategy) and a further multi-round saga on the page side (ending in a structurally different fix: moving the console's real routes off the public URL entirely onto an internal secret-segment path, so middleware simply does nothing on a denial rather than trying to equalize a response -- this pattern, "construct the property so nothing can vary, don't imitate a variable target," became the house approach for this whole class of requirement). All 3 phases are QA-green. docs/plans/platform-manager-console-plan.md has the full defect-by-defect history.

**Client feedback batch** (11 items from a client Word-doc review, comments/Comments.docx, plus a user-authorized scope addition): sidebar/branding shell rebuilt on a new shadcn Sidebar primitive + top-bar brand icon; a /settings hub consolidating 7 scattered settings screens + folding Connector Alerts into MCP Health; a global FieldHint tooltip-help convention rolled out across the whole console; ADR-0009 amended so agent-version authoring/promotion works fully without a Git connection (DB-first, Git becomes an optional enrichment); a shared sandbox/widget chat-preview surface (reused, not a lighter mock, per the project's own "one widget artifact" principle) with a signed short-lived preview token gating who can preview an unpromoted version; a sandbox-test-before-promote gate plus a version "Restore" action; Model Gateway v1's UI reorganized + light model-id validation; an Agent "Design Studio" (a structured-form third authoring mode alongside Text/raw-YAML, always producing/validating the same YAML); a real capability-group picker -- which, under adversarial QA, surfaced a genuine pre-existing gap that toolPolicy.capabilityGroups was never enforced anywhere at runtime (every agent could call every tool in its tenant regardless of its own declared policy) -- the user explicitly authorized building real enforcement (not just fixing the misleading UI copy) as an in-scope addition, which shipped with a defense-in-depth design (pre-filter the tool catalog AND independently re-check at the authorization layer) proven via adversarial splice-testing (breaking either layer alone, confirming the other still catches it). Also, separately in this stretch: a recurring Base-UI-useId()-SSR/CSR-hydration-mismatch bug class was found and fixed in 3 different shared primitives across 3 QA rounds (Collapsible/sidebar, Tooltip/FieldHint, Tabs) before a proactive, user-authorized full-primitive audit closed it for good (finding and fixing a 4th instance, input.tsx, that no prior round had caught, and resolving one previously-untestable risk by constructing a real conversation through the actual product HTTP flow rather than leaving it as a guess). All 11 items plus the enforcement follow-up are QA-green. docs/plans/client-feedback-batch-plan.md has the full round-by-round history.

**Target Architecture Blueprint** (current initiative, user-supplied senior-architecture review + wireframes, docs/blueprint/NextBot-Target-Architecture-Blueprint.md): 6 new modules -- MCP Definition Registry, Knowledge/Graph RAG, Skills + Agent Design Studio, Workflow Designer, Multi-agent Orchestration, Model Gateway v2 -- against an 18-item gap analysis and the blueprint's own 5-phase (0-4) roadmap. Routed through Specification (extended docs/PRODUCT_SPECIFICATION.md/docs/BACKLOG.md, BL-27 through BL-52) -> Architecture (HLD 15, LLD 14, 8 new ADRs 0011-0018 + an ADR-0009 8 amendment) -> a reconciliation pass, since the parallel HLD/LLD dispatches disagreed on one real schema question (capability-group modeling: HLD's single-FK decision won, correctly, since the already-shipped runtime enforcement above depends on it) and left 2 items (graph-DB product, workflow-executor placement) that the reconciliation closed out (Neo4j 5 Enterprise/database-per-tenant; no new workflow-execution service, apps/runtime's existing durable state machine is reused, the only new deployable this wave is nextbot-ingest for the knowledge pipeline) -> Development, now at Phase 6 of 21 (see docs/plans/target-architecture-blueprint-plan.md's Phase status table for the authoritative per-phase list/dependencies).

